  "_doc": "The flame types baked from a Mantaflow fire (tools/textures/fire_sim/bake_flames.py, docs/briefs/fire-look.md 'The next approach'). Each is one simulation: `warm` frames to get going, then 64 + `blend` frames, the last `blend` cross-faded into the first so the sheet loops. Sizes in metres (x across, y depth, z up); `res` the cells along the domain's longest side. `emitter` is a box [x, y, z] of fuel standing on the floor. `domain` and `flow` are Mantaflow's own settings (FluidDomainSettings, FluidFlowSettings), set by name. `turbulence` a turbulence field's strength and size, for the fire's flicker. `squares` the frame's size in the sheet (across, up), the projection resampled to it.",
